Background windows: allow a local companion to run the extension host without showing the workbench.
The extension API cannot control native window visibility at creation time.
This generic CLI flag only suppresses native presentation and focus; all product,
authentication and tool behavior remains in the private extension.
On macOS, background processes use accessory activation to stay out of the Dock.

